From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=A1nos=20Mik=C3=B3?=
 <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 19:44:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 084/154] feat(peek): open a window.open popup as a peek over
 its opener
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Only a normal-type browser was wrapped in an Atrium window, so a popup a
page opened landed in a plain top-level window. The peek route fired on
a link navigation, which window.open never takes. The window now adopts
the contents the browser already built, which is what keeps the opener,
the profile and the storage partition, so a sign-in library still
reaches back by message and still sees the handle close.

An adopted popup shows an origin chip, because the page it lands on is
not the page the user clicked to. The chip follows a redirect, which
every sign-in flow performs. A link-click peek shows no chip.

The caller gives up ownership before the window answers, so opening
returns whether a card took it and hands the contents back when none
did. This also carries three code moves in the window and the controller
that belong to no task in this branch.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc    | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 chrome/browser/ui/tab_helpers.h |  9 +++++++++
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
index fc68f5c8d0b83..b7b01080ce2ef 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
@@ -1710,6 +1710,28 @@ content::WebContents* Browser::AddNewContents(
     }
   }
 
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
+  // A page-opened popup shows as a peek over its opener instead of a window of
+  // its own. `new_contents` is handed over rather than rebuilt, which is what
+  // keeps window.opener and the storage partition.
+
+  // Placed past the fullscreen branches above on purpose: a deferred or
+  // inactive open must not take focus, and the card always does.
+  if (disposition == WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_POPUP &&
+      window_action == NavigateParams::WindowAction::kShowWindow &&
+      atrium::ShouldPeekPopup(
+          this, source, target_url,
+          !window_features.bounds.IsEmpty() && targeting_different_display)) {
+    content::WebContents* peeked = new_contents.get();
+    // A refused adopt hands the popup back, and it falls through to the stock
+    // path below still owned - never destroyed under the caller.
+    new_contents = atrium::AdoptPopupAsPeek(this, std::move(new_contents));
+    if (!new_contents) {
+      return peeked;
+    }
+  }
+#endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
+
   return chrome::AddWebContents(this, source, std::move(new_contents),
                                 target_url, disposition, window_features,
                                 window_action, user_gesture);
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/tab_helpers.h b/chrome/browser/ui/tab_helpers.h
index ec26ac19c0780..89dee76639c96 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/tab_helpers.h
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/tab_helpers.h
@@ -29,6 +29,10 @@ class PreviewTab;
 
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
 
+namespace atrium {
+class BrowserController;
+}
+
 namespace content {
 class WebContents;
 }
@@ -80,6 +84,11 @@ class TabHelpers {
   // Link Preview shows a preview of a page, then promote it as a new tab.
   friend class PreviewTab;
 
+  // The Atrium peek card hosts a page a site opened with window.open, off the
+  // tab strip, and can promote it to a real tab - the same arbitrary external
+  // content the prefetch and preview entries above are friends for.
+  friend class atrium::BrowserController;
+
   // FYI: Do NOT add any more friends here. The functions above are the ONLY
   // ones that need to call AttachTabHelpers; if you think you do, re-read the
   // design document linked above, especially the section "Reusing tab helpers".
